# Portfolio Testing

## Backend

```bash
cd backend
dotnet build
dotnet run
```

Default dev URL: `http://localhost:5000` (check `launchSettings.json`).

| Endpoint | Method | Auth | Expected |
|----------|--------|------|----------|
| `/health` | GET | No | `{ status: "healthy" }` |
| `/api/analytics/visit` | POST | No | 200, JSON body with visit recorded |
| `/api/contact` | POST | No | 400 on empty body; 200 on valid payload |
| `/api/auth/login` | POST | No | 401 on bad creds; JWT on success (dev: `admin` / `admin123`) |
| `/api/analytics/dashboard` | GET | Bearer JWT | 401 without token; stats JSON with token |

## Frontend

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run build
npm run dev
```

- Build must succeed with zero errors
- App loads at `http://localhost:5173/Portfolio_Website/`
- Admin login at `/Portfolio_Website/admin`
- Verify favicon, social icon links, and responsive layout at 375px / 768px widths

## Full smoke test

1. `dotnet build` && `npm run build` — both must pass
2. Start backend, POST a visit, GET dashboard after login
3. Submit contact form with valid data (or expect validation errors)
4. Confirm dashboard shows normalized country/city labels (not raw `"Local"`)
